id: pm-6apl
title: "Native pm ops stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval and test-all with compatible root commands"
description: "Diagnostics and maintenance commands become pm ops <verb> under ADR pm-pbyu: stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, and eval. Each old spelling is alias-shimmed. Keeps validate/health output contracts byte-identical for CI consumers. Duplicate check: no existing ops/diagnostics-namespace item."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:observability",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:34.685Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:17.490Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:16.400Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:16.400Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: pm ops stats/health/validate/gc/telemetry/eval subcommands with flag parity after ADR pm-pbyu acceptance; old spellings alias-shimmed with byte-identical output (CI scripts unaffected); contracts/MCP/completions/docs regenerated; existing specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: Delivered native ops diagnostics and maintenance with compatible root aliases and unchanged SDK/MCP operation identities. Canonical namespace help remains measured under inherited token ceilings; maintained measurement helpers are documented.
expected_result: Ops commands preserve machine-readable results and extension ownership while canonical help stays within existing token ceilings.
actual_result: "Full static gates, linked tests, typecheck, package acceptance and 8639-test exact coverage passed. Canonical help measurements remain below all existing ceilings; baseline values were not relaxed."
