comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T04:24:17.594Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: native command node placement preserves existing SDK handlers; bootstrap aliases, runtime contracts, capability routing, package availability, positional addressing, and three shell completions share declared mappings. TDD reproduced missing namespace support, then verified native/legacy argv and real isolated tracker reads. Broader quality gates and package acceptance are in progress."
  "2026-09-09T04:42:07.069Z","harness:codex","Verification update: focused native/legacy and help/contract suite exercised 271 cases; 270 passed and one obsolete package-hint expectation was corrected. Native JSON help now retains optional-package installation recovery. GitHub live inventory found no open issues or PRs and no open Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts. Full coverage and static gates must finish before closure."
  "2026-09-09T05:05:51.867Z","harness:codex","Distribution and safety evidence: packed local tarball installed independently with npm and Bun; both Node and Bun executed native/legacy CLI parity and imported the new SDK aliases/resolver through both published SDK entrypoints. Bash, Zsh and Fish syntax validation passed; real Fish completion returned native flags with global option values interleaved. Sentry 14-day gate returned critical=0/high=0; secret scan and all three GitHub alert inventories were clear."
  "2026-09-09T05:15:21.025Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked sandbox-safe suite passed 42 tests across 8 files. Repository static gates, duplication checks, typecheck, source documentation coverage, package boundaries, grammar census (187/187), flag invocation parity (84 commands; 3855 flags), token budgets, MCP deprecations, graph composition, and record integrity passed. Native operations preserve existing SDK and MCP identities and machine-readable results."
  "2026-09-09T05:21:01.180Z","harness:codex","Full-coverage run reproduced a docs-skills fixture race: its three-second polling deadline expired before the asynchronous gate emitted JSON, and delayed full-mode output contaminated the next links-only fixture. Replacing this bounded polling assumption with awaiting the actual output completion promise; existing test timeout and all quality thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-09-09T05:29:22.960Z","harness:codex","Final verification: 8639 tests in 655 files passed; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (63818 statements, 48528 branches, 13248 functions, 61196 lines). Full static gates and source documentation requirements passed without relaxed thresholds. Linked suites, typecheck, secret scan, native/legacy temporary-workspace acceptance, real package installation, independent npm/Bun SDK consumers, and npx/bunx packed smoke with 13 packages passed. GitHub issue/PR and security alert inventories were clear before opening this delivery PR."
  "2026-09-09T05:36:31.107Z","harness:codex","Reviewed closeout checks: defect-evidence gate passed with zero findings. Full-population history validation checked 2727 items with zero drift or identity discontinuities. Resolution validation returned its existing warning class for 170 historical records; this delivery records resolution, expected_result, and actual_result atomically for all three selected tasks. Registry confirmed pm-changelog 2026.9.8 latest; package-generated changelog and check passed after a cache-preferred retry for transient npm DNS failures."
  "2026-09-09T05:59:47.138Z","harness:codex","PR 1225 review round 1: CI coverage, static quality, typecheck, compatibility, all OS runtime jobs and hosted analyzers passed. The smoke gate found stale token-baseline command identities next/validate after they moved under namespaces. Correcting discovery to measure canonical core leaves and renaming only those baseline keys while preserving every numeric ceiling. CodeRabbit also identified stronger help/availability/completion assertions and outcome-oriented changelog wording; Sourcery and cubic reported provider quota limits."
  "2026-09-09T16:37:47.785Z","harness:codex","Review correction: canonical context next and ops validate remain measured after their root aliases leave default help. Existing per-command and aggregate ceilings are unchanged; the new ops root has its own bounded baseline. Shortened navigation rationale to fit its inherited ceiling. The 57-surface gate passed. Added regression checks for native help leaves, unavailable optional reindex and installed availability, completion row alignment, and docstrings for touched named functions."
  "2026-09-09T16:43:30.996Z","harness:codex","Release health evidence refreshed: scheduled Auto Release 34324368050 and Release v2026.9.9 run 34326222024 succeeded. Fresh public-registry acceptance of 2026.9.9 passed every declared bin through npx and bunx, including CLI contracts, stdio MCP, HTTP discovery, and missing-bin negative controls. This publication predates PR 1225 and is not publication evidence for the namespace changes."
  "2026-09-09T16:51:31.203Z","harness:codex","Review verification: 8639 tests across 655 files passed, exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (63823 statements, 48528 branches, 13252 functions, 61201 lines). Full static quality, typecheck and the 57-surface token gate passed without relaxed existing ceilings. Each canonical linked namespace suite passed 42 tests; the new token-measurement link passed 12 tests. CodeRabbit accepted the three strengthened test assertions. The latest pm-changelog 2026.9.9 is installed; outcome titles feed package-generated release notes. PR 1225 requires a fresh hosted review on the forthcoming push."
  "2026-09-09T17:17:24.520Z","harness:codex","Review round 2: rejected a proposed baseline reset with measured evidence: ops validate 4158 <= 4870 bytes, context next 2112 <= 2165, ops 1446 <= 1591, total help 231168 <= 251257. Regeneration would raise context next to 2324 bytes, violating the retained-ceiling requirement. Added descriptive JSDoc throughout the maintained measurement script and fixture helpers, and inlined its trivial single-use argument-key wrapper. All touched named callables now have JSDoc according to the TypeScript AST."
  "2026-09-09T17:37:59.350Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first final coverage attempt overlapped full static quality and timed out one existing whole-repository absence-tolerance scan at 30 seconds; 8638 other tests passed. The unchanged focused file then passed all 19 tests in 3.15 seconds. Full static quality completed successfully. A fresh full coverage run is executing alone; no test timeout, exclusion, baseline or coverage threshold was changed."
  "2026-09-09T17:39:15.307Z","harness:codex","Final review correction verification: the isolated full suite passed 8639 tests in 655 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts: 63824 statements, 48530 branches, 13252 functions, 61202 lines. Full static quality and typecheck passed; both items passed both sandboxed linked commands. Real Fish reproduced the original leak and passed context/ctx positives plus focus/next negatives after correction. All touched named callables have descriptive JSDoc by AST inspection; this is scoped evidence, not a repository-wide function-documentation percentage. Every received review artifact was reacted to and replied to; the baseline-reset finding was rejected with unchanged-ceiling measurements. Final hosted verification follows the correction push in PR 1225."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-06T08:04:51.703Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope addition from audit #7 (2026-07-06): include 'test-all' in the ops grouping (workspace-wide linked-test run is a diagnostic, not an item facet). Target verb set becomes: stats, health, validate, gc, telemetry, eval, test-all. See ADR addendum comment on pm-pbyu."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T05:19:57.922Z","harness:codex","When testing CLI orchestration coverage, invoke the instrumented source entrypoint through real transport capture. Executing dist verifies distribution behavior but does not prove source branch coverage."
